---
import { CircleAlertIcon } from '@lucide/astro'
import CodeExample from '@/components/CodeExample.astro'
import ComponentLayout from '@/layouts/ComponentLayout.astro'
import { buildUrl } from '@/scripts/constants'
---

<ComponentLayout name='Ajax Form'>
	<p>
		Use <code>tui-ajax-form</code> for submissions that change server state. It serializes successful
		form controls as URL-encoded data, sends the selected form method, and prevents a full-page navigation.
		Provide an announce target so pending and result messages are available to assistive technology.
	</p>
	<h2>Submit and refresh a view</h2>
	<p>
		The query key connects the form response to any <code>tui-ajax-html</code> view using that same
		key. On success, the form resets by default and the HTML view renders the returned document.
	</p>

	<p>
		Pending text is announced only if the request takes longer than 500 ms. Response-specific
		announce content takes precedence over the configured success or error fallback text.
	</p>
	<CodeExample>
		<tui-ajax-form
			data-tui-query-key='message-list'
			data-tui-announce-id='create-message-status'
		>
			<form method='POST' action={buildUrl('/api/messages')}>
				<div class='form-group'>
					<label for='message-body'>Message</label>
					<textarea id='message-body' name='message' required></textarea>
				</div>
				<div class='action-footer'>
					<button type='submit'>Send message</button>
				</div>
			</form>
			<div id='create-message-status' role='status' class='alert visually-hidden max-w-form'>
			</div>
		</tui-ajax-form>
		<tui-ajax-html id='message-list' class='block' data-tui-query-key='message-list'>
			<p>Messages will appear here.</p>
		</tui-ajax-html>
	</CodeExample>
	<p>
		For server-side validation, nest <code>tui-validate-form</code> inside <code>
			tui-ajax-form
		</code>. Return a <code>422</code> HTML response containing <code>
			template[data-tui-announce]
		</code> and
		<code>form[data-tui-validation-form]</code>. Match controls by <code>id</code> (or by name and
		type) and mark invalid fields with <code>aria-invalid</code>; put each message in an element
		marked <code>data-tui-validation-message</code> and reference its ID from <code>
			aria-describedby
		</code>. The live controls and entered values stay in place, while
		<code>tui-validate-form</code> continues handling correction and resubmission.
	</p>
	<CodeExample>
		<tui-ajax-form data-tui-announce-id='profile-status'>
			<tui-validate-form>
				<form method='POST' action={buildUrl('/api/profile')}>
					<div class='form-group'>
						<label for='profile-email'>Email</label>
						<p id='profile-email-help'>Use an address you can access.</p>
						<input
							id='profile-email'
							name='email'
							type='email'
							required
							aria-describedby='profile-email-help'
						/>
					</div>
					<button type='submit'>Save profile</button>
				</form>
			</tui-validate-form>
			<div id='profile-status' role='status' class='visually-hidden'></div>
		</tui-ajax-form>
	</CodeExample>
	<p>
		Example <code>422</code> response for that form. The current email input is not replaced, so the
		user's entered value remains available to correct.
	</p>
	<CodeExample onlyCode>
		<template data-tui-announce>
			<p>There is 1 error. Review the highlighted field.</p>
		</template>
		<form data-tui-validation-form>
			<div class='form-group'>
				<label for='profile-email'>Email</label>
				<p id='profile-email-help'>Use an address you can access.</p>
				<input
					id='profile-email'
					name='email'
					type='email'
					aria-invalid='true'
					aria-describedby='profile-email-help profile-email-error'
				/>
				<p id='profile-email-error' data-tui-validation-message class='form-message'>
					<CircleAlertIcon aria-hidden='true' />
					<span data-tui-slot='form-message'>This email address is already in use.</span>
				</p>
			</div>
		</form>
	</CodeExample>
	<p>
		The component announces the summary and focuses the first invalid control. On input, the
		validator rechecks that field, removes its server error when valid, and keeps other
		description IDs such as help text. A successful resubmission follows the normal
		success/reset behavior.
	</p>
	<p>
		For successful responses that refresh a view, return status text inside
		<code>template[data-tui-announce]</code>; it is copied into the live region and omitted from
		rendered result markup.
	</p>
	<CodeExample onlyCode>
		<template data-tui-announce>
			<p>Profile saved.</p>
		</template>
		<section id='profile-details'>
			<h2>Profile</h2>
			<p>...</p>
		</section>
	</CodeExample>

	<h2>Keep fields or remove the form</h2>
	<p>
		Set <code>data-tui-keep-fields</code> when the user may need to repeat or revise a submission.
		Set <code>data-tui-action-on-success='remove-form'</code> for one-time forms. Both behaviors apply
		only after a successful response; failed requests leave the form available for correction.
	</p>
	<CodeExample>
		<tui-ajax-form data-tui-announce-id='feedback-status' data-tui-keep-fields>
			<form method='POST' action={buildUrl('/api/messages')}>
				<div class='form-group'>
					<label for='feedback-message'>Feedback</label>
					<textarea id='feedback-message' name='message' required></textarea>
				</div>
				<button type='submit'>Submit feedback</button>
			</form>
			<div id='feedback-status' role='status' class='alert visually-hidden'></div>
		</tui-ajax-form>
	</CodeExample>

	<h2>Options</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><code>data-tui-announce-id</code>: required ID of the status element.</li>
		<li>
			<code>data-tui-query-key</code>: optional key to publish successful response HTML to.
		</li>
		<li><code>data-tui-keep-fields</code>: do not reset fields after success.</li>
		<li>
			<code>data-tui-action-on-success='remove-form'</code>: remove this component after
			success.
		</li>
		<li>
			<code>data-tui-message-submitting</code>, <code>data-tui-message-success</code>, and <code
			>
				data-tui-message-error
			</code>: customize status text.
		</li>
	</ul>
</ComponentLayout>
